1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,599
Begin in New Call with a
clearly named training exercise.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,220
Complete Name and Nature, then choose
the department’s Priority and Type.

3
00:00:08,619 --> 00:00:13,020
Here, Urgent and Structure Fire match
the prepared Academy Training Alarm.

4
00:00:13,449 --> 00:00:17,600
A run card is configured beforehand
in Core administration; the dispatch

5
00:00:17,629 --> 00:00:19,329
app uses that configuration.

6
00:00:19,819 --> 00:00:24,389
Enter and check the incident’s Latitude
and Longitude before comparing resources.

7
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:28,270
These are fictional incident
coordinates, not a device location.

8
00:00:28,709 --> 00:00:32,599
The first exercise stays unsent
while we inspect its recommendation.

9
00:00:32,959 --> 00:00:37,459
This browser recording cannot establish
native background GPS collection or

10
00:00:37,459 --> 00:00:39,750
delivery of an alert to a real device.

11
00:00:39,869 --> 00:00:43,550
Under Dispatch To, read the
named card and its Decision.

12
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:47,129
The rule asks whether an
engine is within eight minutes.

13
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:52,940
The first preview says Yes: Engine 51
has an estimated two-minute response.

14
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:56,510
That does not mean the entire
response package is complete.

15
00:00:56,979 --> 00:01:01,450
Ideal configuration not available
and Could not fill explain that the

16
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:03,819
incident-officer positions are too old.

17
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:07,110
Read the explanation before
accepting a proposal.

18
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:11,520
An available vehicle and an eligible
officer are separate requirements.

19
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:15,549
The advice to send the initial response
is guidance from this configured

20
00:01:15,549 --> 00:01:19,549
card; it is not proof that resources
have already been dispatched.

21
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:23,739
For the next preview, the three
unchanged fictional officers received

22
00:01:23,739 --> 00:01:27,350
fresh simulated station fixes through
the controlled training setup.

23
00:01:27,759 --> 00:01:32,680
Their statuses and earlier history
were preserved; no device GPS was used.

24
00:01:33,129 --> 00:01:38,319
The refreshed proposal now lists Engine
51 under Recommended units and Christopher

25
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:40,399
Herrmann under Recommended personnel.

26
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:45,050
The Fills labels explain which package
requirement each resource satisfies.

27
00:01:45,499 --> 00:01:49,610
Read both rows and their reasons,
then choose Apply recommendation.

28
00:01:50,069 --> 00:01:52,099
The form changes to two selected.

29
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:56,709
Applying the proposal prepares a
selection; it does not create the call.

30
00:01:57,110 --> 00:02:01,310
Open that selection to inspect the actual
people and units before proceeding.

31
00:02:01,469 --> 00:02:07,010
The Select Dispatch Recipients sheet
offers Closest, Name and Available only.

32
00:02:07,429 --> 00:02:10,280
Closest follows the server’s
location-aware board.

33
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:14,460
Herrmann appears with Nearest
number one and the Run card badge.

34
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:20,149
Name changes the order; Blake Gallo then
appears with Unavailable and No location.

35
00:02:20,579 --> 00:02:23,960
The absence of a location
is useful information, not

36
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,349
an invitation to guess one.

37
00:02:25,839 --> 00:02:29,950
Available only reduces this example
from fourteen users to twelve.

38
00:02:30,399 --> 00:02:34,539
Previously selected recipients remain
selected, so review the checkmarks

39
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:36,300
and total as well as the filter.

40
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:39,030
Everyone is a broader recipient choice.

41
00:02:39,469 --> 00:02:43,039
Leave it clear when this exercise
needs only named resources.

42
00:02:43,239 --> 00:02:45,529
Search for Engine to narrow the sheet.

43
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:49,719
The Groups entry called Engine
51 and the unit called Engine

44
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:51,689
51 are separate choices.

45
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:55,660
In this example the group is
unchecked and the unit is checked.

46
00:02:56,069 --> 00:02:59,919
Read the unit’s Available status,
Herrmann’s crew assignment and

47
00:03:00,079 --> 00:03:01,740
At station position source.

48
00:03:02,089 --> 00:03:05,230
Its Nearest number three badge
is its place among the board’s

49
00:03:05,230 --> 00:03:09,169
available units; it does not say
that three engines are selected.

50
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,259
The row shows an estimated travel
time, while the board can rank

51
00:03:13,259 --> 00:03:15,260
units using turnout plus travel.

52
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:18,880
Confirm returns the selected
recipients to the call form.

53
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:22,299
It is still separate from
creating or dispatching the call.

54
00:03:22,539 --> 00:03:25,730
Changing only the unsent
incident’s coordinates creates

55
00:03:25,730 --> 00:03:27,110
the distant comparison.

56
00:03:27,539 --> 00:03:30,839
The same engine now fails the
eight-minute condition, and the

57
00:03:30,839 --> 00:03:33,200
outcome becomes Review alternatives.

58
00:03:33,610 --> 00:03:36,879
The advice-only branch
recommends no additional package.

59
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:40,879
The recipient sheet shows about one
hundred and one kilometres and roughly

60
00:03:40,879 --> 00:03:44,600
one hundred and ninety-eight minutes
for both Herrmann and Engine 51.

61
00:03:45,119 --> 00:03:48,779
The run-card response estimate is
slightly longer because its response

62
00:03:48,779 --> 00:03:50,490
calculation includes turnout.

63
00:03:50,879 --> 00:03:53,660
These are estimates, not
a promise of arrival.

64
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:58,070
Notice that the earlier two selected
recipients remain in the form even

65
00:03:58,070 --> 00:03:59,730
when the recommendation changes.

66
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:04,270
Restore the near coordinates and review
both the new decision and your selection.

67
00:04:04,399 --> 00:04:08,970
For the saved example, a separate
call named TRAINING ONLY, Dispatch

68
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:12,229
allocation recording was created
with those same two fictional

69
00:04:12,229 --> 00:04:14,469
recipients after checking every field.

70
00:04:15,019 --> 00:04:18,849
Open Dispatched to inspect what
the application stored: Herrmann

71
00:04:18,849 --> 00:04:21,770
as a user and Engine 51 as a unit.

72
00:04:22,299 --> 00:04:26,369
Dispatch additional resources opens
the existing call’s recommendation.

73
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:30,000
Its banner says the decision was
pinned from the dispatcher’s preview,

74
00:04:30,369 --> 00:04:33,910
and the explanation counts the engine
and officer already on the call.

75
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:37,269
Zero additional recommendations
can mean the existing

76
00:04:37,269 --> 00:04:38,980
allocation covers the package.

77
00:04:39,339 --> 00:04:43,530
Strike alarm two is visible, but this
training card has only one configured

78
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:46,240
level, so no escalation is exercised here.

79
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:49,120
Re-evaluate requests
a current calculation.

80
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:54,570
Here it returns No and Review
alternatives after ordinary call creation

81
00:04:54,570 --> 00:04:56,420
changed the engine to Responding.

82
00:04:56,839 --> 00:05:00,960
Treat this as a fresh assessment,
not another dispatch or evidence

83
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,850
that the earlier recipients vanished.

84
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:05,389
Cancel the picker without adding anyone.

85
00:05:05,910 --> 00:05:11,270
To finish this disposable exercise, Close
Call uses Closed, a training note, and

86
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:13,570
Notify everyone on the call switched off.

87
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:15,690
Only this new call was closed.

88
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:19,960
The console returned to the original
three active calls, and Activity

89
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:23,559
records the engine’s normal change
from Responding to Released.

90
00:05:24,039 --> 00:05:28,080
Awaiting Resources is a separate queue
for outstanding requirements; the

91
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:32,390
captured queue is empty, so no requirement
fulfilment or dismissal is claimed.

